    <p class="tag">Specialised Service</p>
    <h1>Exit Clearance &amp; Departure Requirements</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Confirm what you need before you leave the Philippines, not at the departure gate.</p>

    <p>Foreign nationals who have stayed in the Philippines for an extended period, or who hold certain long-term visas, may need to obtain clearance from the Bureau of Immigration before departing. Foreign Immigration Services helps you confirm what applies to you and coordinates the clearance process.</p>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirming whether an exit clearance applies to your situation</li>
      <li>Preparing and organising the required documentation</li>
      <li>Coordinating the clearance application with the Bureau of Immigration</li>
      <li>Advising on related matters — such as an outstanding extension or a visa downgrade — before you depart</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Common Situations We Handle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Departing after a long-term stay in the Philippines</li>
      <li>Holding a long-term visa and travelling temporarily, with plans to return</li>
      <li>Needing to resolve an outstanding immigration matter before leaving</li>
      <li>Other departure-related circumstances</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Initial enquiry</h3>
        <p>Tell us your visa status and travel plans.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Assessment</h3>
        <p>We confirm whether a clearance applies to your situation, and which type.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Preparation</h3>
        <p>We help you prepare the documentation your clearance requires.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Submission and follow-up</h3>
        <p>We coordinate the application and keep you informed ahead of your departure.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="context-note">
      <p>Whether an exit clearance is required, and which type, depends on your visa category and length of stay — we confirm this as part of the assessment.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="service-cta">
      <h2>Confirm Your Departure Requirements</h2>
      <p>Tell us your travel plans and current visa status, and we will confirm what applies to you.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?service=exit-clearance">Request Exit Clearance Assistance</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need an exit clearance every time I leave?</summary>
        <p>It depends on your visa status and how long you've been in the Philippines. Tell us your situation and we'll confirm whether it applies to your upcoming departure.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if I've overstayed and need to leave?</summary>
        <p>This is a common and manageable situation. See our <a href="/services/immigration-status-review-and-regularisation/">Immigration Status Review</a> service, or tell us your travel plans directly and we'll advise on the right order of steps.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

